// dsv4-arena-sim.bml -- how big the expert arena should be: the experts a real run picked (a token-run receipt row's "picks"), replayed through the cache the arena runs at other slot counts.
//
//   echo '{}' | ./fkwu observe/dsv4-arena-sim.bml          the LAST row of receipts/dsv4-token-runs.jsonl: the fit of its wall against the experts its warm decode tokens missed (ms an expert's fill costs, the fixed ms),
//                                                             then for 64, 80, 96, 128, 160, 192 and 256 slots a layer: the arena's size, the share of the experts it holds, the warm decode hit rate and the experts
//                                                             missed and MB filled a token, the prefill's misses. Reads the receipt and the file's header; opens nothing, maps nothing, writes nothing, takes no lease.
//   options (one JSON line on stdin): receipt (receipts/dsv4-token-runs.jsonl), row (the line, 0 first; the last by default), file (the IQ2XXS build by default; only its header is read)
//
// The picks are in a row when the token door recorded them (it does by default; {"picks":0} turns it off); a row of an older run carries none and this says so. The replay is the arena's own cache (dsv4-expert-cache.bml),
// proven equal to the real arena's counts row by row on the fixtures (native/metal/tests/dsv4-arena-sim-band.bml). Every rule, row and number is a definition of form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-arena-sim.bml.
